<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13814" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-στᾰτέον</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφίσταμαι</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one must stand off from,</i>
			i.e. <i>give up, abandon,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολέμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					8.2
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ . . ἀ. τῇ πόλει τούτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.199
				</span></i>
			: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀ. πρίν . .</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Plt.</u>
					257c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> later,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ʽἁ̓φίστημι</span>
			<i>one must keep apart, detain,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππον ἀπὸ τῶν ἔργων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Gp.</u>
					16.1.4
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
